{"id": "EUVD-2026-103567", "enisaUuid": "eafcef50-0e30-30cf-852d-a1b23884297a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: Fix _gaccess_shadow_fault()\n\nIn some circumstances, it is possible that the page of nested guest\nmemory that is being shadowed is not present at all in the parent guest\ngmap. dat_entry_walk() will not find any leaf entry and return with\n-ENOENT, which will erroneously be propagated all the way to userspace.\n\nFix by manually calling gmap_link() on the memory of the nested guest\nthat is being shadowed if the mapping was not already present.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94c43c7df46433ed4d1e18f13770b019ba977bd8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/faff4c8ff3dbec6d71b89dd281a0d17c4478fa44"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v97x-654r-4f82", "CVE-2026-98653"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00981727-a344-31c9-ae15-43ab8f282928", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2072608a-a73d-3666-b32d-e3f1a74972b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2bca4bc3-6040-3e6b-9cbb-03223a37385c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "4b801b1c-b295-3379-b98b-eb84e48af0f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "60712b23-6350-382f-a24e-37617295bee0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e38c884df92119d96f652d51f82661dd2fc0b885 <faff4c8ff3dbec6d71b89dd281a0d17c4478fa44"}, {"id": "97cacd10-f608-3254-8bdf-cf9e34a6f82c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e38c884df92119d96f652d51f82661dd2fc0b885 <94c43c7df46433ed4d1e18f13770b019ba977bd8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{